    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0838" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg710"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 532.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Foster</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 332.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuance of former correspondence on
                    the subject of the so-called cattle-tax exacted on exports from Key West, by the
                    Spanish consul there, I have to inclose a copy of a letter from Messrs. McGrew
                    &amp; Small, attorneys of James McKay and other exporters, who have paid such
                    taxes, making a request as to the mode or channel of the promised refunding of
                    said taxes. The adoption of their suggestion lies, of course, with His Majesty’s
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d532-a1.xml" xpointer="d532-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
